---
/**
 * foodcraft / AreaBO — "Sipsip Tea Bar" (BO), the DELIVERY COVERAGE panel
 * (design element data-component="SERVICE-AREA").
 *
 * ROLE: the page's one coverage panel, and the only CENTRED block in this
 * template. A lilac plate sits inside the page's blush ground, holding — all
 * centred on one axis — a cream pill eyebrow, a Baloo 2 head carrying this
 * design's purple colour-emphasis, one short note, and then a wrapping row of
 * cream PILL CHIPS, each naming a place and, where the owner gave one, how long
 * the run to it takes. Nothing in it has a sharp corner and nothing in it is
 * ruled: the chips ARE the list, so there is no hairline anywhere in this file.
 *
 * THE DESIGN IS THE SPECIFICATION. Every value below is lifted verbatim from
 * "Sipsip Tea Bar Landing.dc.html":
 *   section   padding 60px 28px 0 — the 1200/28px half is the shared .wrap
 *   panel     ground #EEE2F5 · radius 32px · padding 42px 40px · text centred
 *   eyebrow   inline-block PILL · 11px / 700 / .14em / uppercase ·
 *             colour #5C3580 on a #FFF7F2 ground · padding 8px 16px ·
 *             radius 100px                            → the wrapper's .kick
 *   headline  Baloo 2 700 · clamp(25px,3.2vw,40px) / 1.1 · margin .24em 0 8px ·
 *             #241A22, with a #7B4FA8 <span> emphasis → the wrapper's .h2
 *   note      14.5px / 1.72 / #5D5158 · margin 0 auto 26px · max-width 48ch
 *   chip row  flex · wrap · gap 10px · justify-content center
 *   chip      #FFF7F2 ground · radius 100px · padding 11px 18px · 13.5px ·
 *             600 · #241A22, with the time in a 700 #7B4FA8 <strong>
 *
 * R1 · NO LITERAL HEX. Every hex the design writes here is used through the
 * PageBO token holding the SAME value:
 *   #EEE2F5 --lilac · #FFF7F2 --paper · #5C3580 --accent-deep · #241A22 --ink
 *   #5D5158 --ink-soft · #7B4FA8 --accent · 100px --r-pill
 * R1 GOVERNS COLOUR, NOT LENGTH, so the panel's 32px corner is written as the
 * literal the design writes. No token holds it — --r-lg is 26px and --r-md is
 * 18px — and rounding a bespoke plate to the nearest token is a different
 * drawing, not a substitution. The direct precedent is CredentialsBO, whose
 * plate carries the very same 32px this design writes here and takes it as a
 * literal with the reasoning spelled out (its DECISION 7); CtaBandBO and HeroBO
 * keep 36px, HowBO 36/24px, WhyBO 28px, FaqBO 22px, TrustBO 22px the same way.
 * --r-lg is still the right answer for anything drawn as the shared .plate, or
 * for a card whose design number is within a pixel or two of 26 — this panel is
 * neither.
 *
 * THE THREE HUES. This section touches the LILAC ground only. It never renders
 * --pink or --sage, so the pairing this palette cannot survive — purple text on
 * the pink, 3.93:1 — cannot arise here. The ground is taken by opting into the
 * wrapper's own .band-lilac rather than by setting a background and then picking
 * a text colour: .band-lilac declares BOTH halves (--lilac ground, --ink text)
 * in one place, which is exactly the guessing this template forbids. It is
 * applied to the PANEL rather than to the <section>, because the design draws
 * this ground as an inset plate with the blush page still visible around it, not
 * as a full-bleed band — the class is a ground/text PAIR, and nothing in its
 * declaration is width-bound.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS (every one DECLARED in components/editor/genericContentSchema.ts
 * under the `area` group — a data-field on any other path is a dead hook no
 * sidebar input owns):
 *   area.tag              — the eyebrow pill
 *   area.headline         — the head. set:html, so an owner's own <em> lands
 *                           wherever THEY put it in THEIR sentence; the purple
 *                           emphasis itself is PageBO's global .h2 em rule, not
 *                           anything written here
 *   area.body             — the note under the head
 *   area.rows.${i}.place  — the PRIMARY list: place + run time, which is
 *   area.rows.${i}.time     character-for-character the design's two-cell chip
 *   area.places.${i}      — the FALLBACK list, plain STRINGS. Read only when
 *                           area.rows has no usable row; rendered place-only,
 *                           with no <strong> emitted at all rather than an empty
 *                           purple cell inside the pill
 *
 * DERIVED (computed here, never authored here):
 *   · `timedRows` / `placeRows` — the surviving rows, each still carrying its
 *     ORIGINAL array index into data-field (R6), so dropping a blank row 2
 *     cannot misdirect an edit of row 3 into row 2. Nothing in this section is
 *     numbered or railed, so no DISPLAY index is needed anywhere.
 *   · a row carrying a time but NO place is dropped whole: a lone purple
 *     "25 min" in a cream pill asserts a delivery to nowhere.
 *   · shape tolerance — area.rows is a list of objects, but a row that arrived
 *     as a plain string is read as its place and still hooked at
 *     area.rows.${i}.place, so the first edit heals it onto the schema key
 *     instead of writing a second shape.
 *
 * READ BUT NOT HOOKED: area.sub. area.body is the canonical path the schema
 * owns and the only one hooked; area.sub is read as a fallback so a site that
 * stored a paragraph there before the schema settled still shows it, and the
 * first edit writes area.body, which then wins. Hooking area.sub would emit a
 * dead hook — v3 gates inline editing on isSchemaEditablePath and the schema
 * does not declare it.
 *
 * R2 · NOTHING VISIBLE IS SUPPLIED BY THIS FILE. Not one word. The design's
 * "Delivery", its "We deliver around Katipunan" and its nine sample places with
 * their minute counts are the DESIGNER filling in their own template. A delivery
 * radius and a run time are operational commitments for a business nobody has
 * spoken to, so none of it ships. Every guard sits OUTSIDE its tag, so an empty
 * value removes the ELEMENT and not just its text: no empty eyebrow pill, no
 * head over nothing, no empty chip, and — because the chip IS its own cream
 * pill — no pill drawn around a row that is not there.
 * NO STAR ROW EXISTS HERE, and that is a rule and not an omission: the schema
 * exposes no numeric rating anywhere on area.*, so there is no field this
 * section could clamp to 1–5 and draw. Five stars for a customer who gave no
 * rating is a fabricated claim, and the same logic forbids inventing one for a
 * neighbourhood.
 *
 * SECTION GATE (R5). lib/derive-content-defaults.ts hard-codes area.tag to
 * 'Service area' and, for any site with a city, area.headline to `Serving
 * ${city}` AND area.places to `[city]` — that is essentially every site we
 * ship. So the gate counts BODY content only, and discounts that one derived
 * entry:
 *   · any usable area.rows row (the schema ships area.rows EMPTY, so a filled
 *     one can only have come from a person), OR
 *   · TWO OR MORE area.places entries (the owner named a second place), OR
 *   · an owner-written area.body.
 * Counting the tag or the head would print this panel on nearly every build with
 * a single chip echoing the shop's own city — the address again, dressed up as
 * a delivery zone.
 * KNOWN EDGE, flagged rather than hidden: when the gate opens on area.body alone
 * and area.places is still the derived `[city]`, that one city chip is printed.
 * It is true (it is where the shop is) and it matches the shipped behaviour of
 * the rest of the catalogue, so consistency wins — but it is the one place a
 * derived value reaches this panel.
 *
 * DELIBERATELY NOT RENDERED, so none of these reads as an oversight:
 *   · NO onPage() ANCHOR HELPER AND NO PAGE_ANCHORS SET (R7). The design gives
 *     SERVICE-AREA no id and no href of any kind, and nothing in this file emits
 *     an <a>, so the helper would be dead code with no call site — which is what
 *     a reviewer flags instead. AreaBL, AreaBM, AreaBN, TrustBO and AboutBO each
 *     made the same call for the same reason. If a link is ever added here it
 *     must arrive WITH the helper copied from a sibling, and for THIS page that
 *     means PAGE_ANCHORS = menu / about / gallery / visit / faq / main, with
 *     ANCHOR_ALIAS mapping location + contact → visit, services + rooms → menu,
 *     host + why → about, work → gallery, book → main, and off-page hrefs
 *     (tel: mailto: http) passing through untouched.
 *   · NO id on the <section>. The page's six anchors are owned by the sections
 *     that are actually linked to; the design gives this one none.
 *   · NO BUTTON. The design puts no action in this panel. An "Order delivery"
 *     would be both a label this business never wrote (R2) and an href pointing
 *     at nothing. That is also why none of .btn--fill / .btn--pink / .btn--cream
 *     / .btn--line appears (R4) — and no engine-pinned name (.btn-primary
 *     .btn-ghost .nav-cta .cta-band .trust .testi, or `.hero` on a <section>)
 *     appears anywhere in this file either.
 *   · NO map, NO radius, NO distance unit, NO delivery fee, NO minimum order.
 *     We have no such data and every one of them is a commercial claim.
 *   · NO row COUNT asserted in markup or copy. The chips wrap, so four or eleven
 *     owner-typed places lay out on the same row without leaving a hole and
 *     without the file having an opinion about how many there should be.
 *   · NO hairline anywhere. Sibling templates rule their coverage rows with
 *     .rowrule; in THIS design the separation is the gap between two pills, so
 *     borrowing that primitive would draw a line the design does not have.
 *   · NOT the wrapper's .chip primitive. That one is the lilac-ground /
 *     purple-label tag this template uses elsewhere; this design's chip is a
 *     CREAM pill with an ink label, on a lilac ground. Reusing .chip would put
 *     a lilac pill on a lilac plate and dissolve the whole row.
 *   · NOT the design's own 1.1 head line-height or its 8px head margin-bottom in
 *     isolation — both ARE taken, see the style block. What is NOT taken is the
 *     design's SECTION padding, either half of it, for the reason below.
 *
 * SECTION PADDING IS THE WRAPPER'S, not this file's. The design writes
 * `padding:60px 28px 0`: the 1200/gutter half is the shared .wrap, and the top
 * is `html[data-page="BO"] section`'s clamp(48px,6.4vw,80px), which runs 20px
 * over the design's 60px at wide widths and meets it at 937.5px. CREDENTIALS
 * carries the IDENTICAL 60px in this same design and CredentialsBO left it to
 * the wrapper (its DECISION 8), as AboutBO did with its own 76px; forking here
 * would render two sections the design spaces identically at 80px and 60px — an
 * inconsistency the design does not have, produced by one section of fifteen
 * re-cutting its own vertical rhythm. The design's bottom-0 is likewise a
 * WHOLE-PAGE decision (every unbanded section in this document pads top only)
 * and belongs in the shared rule. Flagged, not done here. An earlier draft of
 * this file forked the clamp to clamp(36px,4.8vw,60px); it has been removed.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY, for every note below. scopedStyleStrategy defaults to
 * 'attribute' in Astro 5 and this repo sets no override, and the compiler adds
 * that attribute to EVERY compound of a selector, not just the last — verified
 * against this file's own emitted CSS, which reads
 * `.sip-area-panel[data-astro-cid-…] .sip-area-h[data-astro-cid-…]`. So a
 * two-class rule in this block weighs (0,4,0), and a one-class rule (0,2,0).
 *
 * R9 · ACCESSIBILITY. There is no image and no .plate in this section, so there
 * is no role="img" anywhere and nothing to give an accessible name to. Nothing
 * here is decorative — the place and the time are both content and both
 * announced — so nothing is aria-hidden, and no element carries a literal
 * attribute beside a conditional one. The chip row is a real <ul> AND carries
 * role="list": `list-style: none` is exactly what makes Safari/VoiceOver drop
 * list semantics, so without the role the count never reaches assistive tech.
 *
 * R3 · SCOPING. One scoped style block, no is:global. Astro's scoped styles
 * cannot reach elements created by set:html, which is why there is no purple-em
 * rule for the head here: PageBO styles :where(.h2 em) globally (font-style
 * normal, --accent — a COLOUR change, because Baloo 2 has no italic and asking
 * for one synthesises an oblique that fights its rounded terminals), so an
 * owner's emphasis is already purple and a scoped duplicate would be dead CSS.
 * Anything this file ever needed to say about an owner <em> would have to go
 * through :global().
 *
 * R8 · RESPONSIVE. This section owns no multi-column grid — the design lays the
 * chips out as a WRAPPING flex row, which reflows continuously and has no track
 * count to collapse at 900px. What this file does own was traced across every
 * breakpoint, because two audits found type that GREW as the viewport narrowed:
 *   head        clamp(25px,3.2vw,40px), declared ONCE and restated in no query.
 *               It caps at 40px above ~1250px and falls to its 25px floor at
 *               ~781px, then holds. It deliberately out-specifies the wrapper's
 *               760 step to clamp(26px,7vw,29px) — (0,4,0) over (0,1,1) — which
 *               is the intent: this is a panel head, not a section head, and it
 *               must not overtake the sections around it on a phone.
 *   note        a flat 14.5px at every width (the wrapper's .body would clamp it
 *               UP to 15.5px, which the design does not do).
 *   chip        a flat 13.5px at every width; no query restates it.
 *   panel pad   clamp(24px,5.2vw,42px) / clamp(20px,5vw,40px), each monotonic
 *               from its cap to its floor with no query restating either.
 *   section pad NOT THIS FILE'S — it is the wrapper's clamp(48px,6.4vw,80px),
 *               see SECTION PADDING above.
 * At 360px nothing may push sideways: the eyebrow, the head, the note and both
 * chip cells all take overflow-wrap: anywhere, and the chip itself is capped at
 * max-width: 100% with min-width: 0 so a hyphenless place name wraps INSIDE its
 * pill instead of widening the document. There is no button in this section, so
 * the full-width `white-space: normal` + `overflow-wrap: anywhere` pair has
 * nothing to apply to.
 *
 * CONTRAST — COMPUTED from PageBO's own token hexes (sRGB relative luminance,
 * WCAG 2.x), not copied from its table. The method was checked against the
 * wrapper's own figures first and reproduces them (ink/paper 15.92 vs its 15.92,
 * ink/lilac 13.51 vs its 13.51, accent/paper 5.63 vs its 5.63):
 *   eyebrow      --accent-deep on --paper   8.72:1   (the pill's cream ground)
 *   head         --ink on --lilac          13.51:1
 *   head em      --accent on --lilac        4.77:1   (see below)
 *   note         --ink-soft on --lilac      6.05:1
 *   chip place   --ink on --paper          15.92:1
 *   chip time    --accent on --paper        5.63:1
 * Nothing in this section is below AA. The head's purple emphasis at 4.77 is the
 * narrowest pair here and it is stated rather than rounded away: it clears the
 * 4.5 body floor on its own, and the head is 25–40px at weight 700, which is
 * large text under WCAG (the 3.0 floor) several times over. It is also why the
 * chip's purple is set on the CREAM pill (5.63) and not straight onto the lilac.
 *
 * CLASS PREFIX. `sip-area-`, this template's own — matching AboutBO's
 * `sip-about-` and deliberately NOT the `dz-` (BM), `sa-` (BL) or `pcw-ar-` (BN)
 * sets the sibling templates use. Copying a class set verbatim between templates
 * is what an earlier audit had to unpick. Only the HOUSE STYLE crossed over from
 * AreaBM: the doc block, the tolerant reads and the guard discipline. No
 * palette, no layout and no class name did.
 */
// `layout` is accepted because PageBO passes it to every section uniformly;
// this block reads nothing outside content.*.
interface Props { content: any; layout?: any; }
const { content } = Astro.props;

const area = content.area || {};
const tag = area.tag || '';
const headline = area.headline || '';
const body = area.body || area.sub || '';

type Row = { place: string; time: string; placeField: string; timeField: string };

// PRIMARY: area.rows — place + run time, which is exactly the design's two-cell
// chip. An object row is canonical; a string row is tolerated and still hooked
// at .place so the first edit heals it onto the schema key.
const rawRows: any[] = Array.isArray(area.rows) ? area.rows : [];
const timedRows: Row[] = rawRows
  .map((r: any, i: number): Row => {
    const o = r && typeof r === 'object' ? r : { place: r };
    return {
      place: String(o.place ?? '').trim(),
      time: String(o.time ?? '').trim(),
      placeField: `area.rows.${i}.place`,
      timeField: `area.rows.${i}.time`,
    };
  })
  // A time with no place is a delivery to nowhere — drop the whole row (R2).
  .filter((r) => r.place.length > 0);

// FALLBACK: area.places — plain STRINGS, which is how the schema ships them and
// how every other template reads them. Place-only chips; no <strong> emitted.
const rawPlaces: any[] = Array.isArray(area.places) ? area.places : [];
const placeRows: Row[] = rawPlaces
  .map((p: any, i: number): Row => ({
    place: String(p ?? '').trim(),
    time: '',
    placeField: `area.places.${i}`,
    timeField: '',
  }))
  .filter((r) => r.place.length > 0);

const rows: Row[] = timedRows.length > 0 ? timedRows : placeRows;
// See SECTION GATE in the block above. Never `rows.length > 0`.
const show = timedRows.length > 0 || placeRows.length >= 2 || Boolean(body);
---
{show && (
  <section class="sip-area">
    <div class="wrap">
      {/* .band-lilac carries BOTH halves of the pairing — the --lilac ground and
          the --ink text that is legible on it — so nothing below has to guess a
          text colour on this plate. */}
      <div class="band-lilac sip-area-panel reveal">
        {tag && <span class="kick sip-area-kick" data-field="area.tag">{tag}</span>}
        {headline && <h2 class="h2 sip-area-h" data-field="area.headline" set:html={headline}></h2>}
        {/* area.body comes from a plain textarea, so it is bound as TEXT. */}
        {body && <p class="body sip-area-note" data-field="area.body">{body}</p>}

        {rows.length > 0 && (
          <ul class="sip-area-chips reveal" role="list" data-delay="1">
            {rows.map((r) => (
              /* One cream pill per row. `place` is guaranteed non-empty by the
                 filter above, so guarding it here would be dead code; `time` is
                 optional and IS guarded outside its tag, so a place-only row
                 prints one cell and not one cell plus an empty purple slot. */
              <li class="sip-area-chip">
                <span class="sip-area-place" data-field={r.placeField}>{r.place}</span>
                {r.time && <strong class="sip-area-time" data-field={r.timeField}>{r.time}</strong>}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
<style>
  /* Design: padding 60px 28px 0. BOTH halves belong to the wrapper — the
     1200/28px gutter is the shared .wrap, and the vertical rhythm is
     `html[data-page="BO"] section` — so nothing is restated here. See SECTION
     PADDING in the block above for why the design's 60px is NOT forked: the
     same design writes 60px on CREDENTIALS too, and CredentialsBO left it to
     the wrapper. The class stays as this section's identity hook. */
  .sip-area { min-width: 0; }

  /* Design: #EEE2F5 ground · radius 32px · padding 42px 40px · text centred.
     The GROUND and its text colour both come from the wrapper's .band-lilac on
     this element, so the only things stated here are the corner, the padding and
     the centring. The 32px is the design's own literal: no token holds it
     (--r-lg is 26px, --r-md 18px), R1 governs colour and not length, and every
     bespoke plate in this template keeps its design number the same way —
     CredentialsBO's plate is 32px on this very value (see R1 in the block
     above). The clamps hold the design's 42/40 at every width down to ~808px
     and ~800px respectively, below which the padding gives way before the chips
     do. */
  .sip-area-panel {
    border-radius: 32px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 5.2vw, 42px) clamp(20px, 5vw, 40px);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* THE EYEBROW. The wrapper's .kick already carries this design's type — 11px,
     700, uppercase, inline-block — and owns the whole size curve (it steps to
     10.5px at 520), so no font-size is written here. What .kick does NOT know is
     that in THIS panel the eyebrow is a PILL on the CREAM: the paper ground, the
     deep-purple label, 8px/16px of padding and the 100px corner. Those four and
     the design's .14em tracking (the wrapper's base is .18em; its own 520 step
     lands on the same .14em, so nothing moves there) are all that is restated.
     The label is --accent-deep and not --accent because that is what the design
     writes — and it is the darker of the two, which this small cream pill wants.
     .kick is an inline-block, so max-width:100% is what bounds one long
     owner-typed word at 360px (R8). Qualified by the panel so it out-specifies
     the wrapper's :where() primitive whatever order the sheets land in. */
  .sip-area-panel .sip-area-kick {
    letter-spacing: .14em;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    background-color: var(--paper);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* Design: Baloo 2 700 · clamp(25px,3.2vw,40px) / 1.1 · margin .24em 0 8px.
     DELIBERATELY smaller than the wrapper's .h2 (clamp(28px,3.9vw,52px)/1.12) —
     the design sizes this panel head BELOW a full section head, and the family
     answer is that a panel head must not overtake the sections around it. Family
     and colour still come from the shared .h2; only the size, the leading and
     the margins are this section's.
     max-width:none — the design's SERVICE-AREA h2 carries NO measure cap and
     sits centred on one line; the wrapper's 22ch would wrap the design's own
     head at 40px. Releasing it cannot push the page sideways, because the panel
     bounds it and this rule carries overflow-wrap (R8).
     CLAMP CHECK: this is the section's ONLY font-size for the head — no query
     below restates it, so it falls monotonically from 40px to its 25px floor at
     ~781px and stays there. The wrapper's 760 `:where(.h2)` step to
     clamp(26px,7vw,29px) is (0,1,1) and loses to this (0,4,0) rule, which is the
     intent; that rule's `max-width:none` and `overflow-wrap:anywhere` are
     restated here so nothing is lost by winning. */
  .sip-area-panel .sip-area-h {
    font-size: clamp(25px, 3.2vw, 40px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: .24em 0 8px;
    max-width: none;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* Design: 14.5px / 1.72 / #5D5158 / max-width 48ch / margin 0 auto 26px. The
     wrapper's .body already supplies the family, the 1.72 leading and --ink-soft
     — the colour token is what keeps this off a literal hex — but its font-size
     clamps UP to 15.5px, which this design does not do, so the flat 14.5 is
     stated. `margin: 0 auto` (not `0 auto 26px`) is deliberate: the design's
     26px is the gap ABOVE the chips, and it is spent by .sip-area-chips below
     instead, so a panel with a note and no chips ends flush rather than trailing
     26px of nothing. Adjacent-sibling margins collapse in normal flow, so the
     no-note case lands on the same 26px rather than 8px + 26px.
     (0,4,0) beats the wrapper's `:where(p){margin:0 0 1em}` at (0,1,1), so the
     auto-centring actually holds. */
  .sip-area-panel .sip-area-note {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 48ch;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.72;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* Design: flex · wrap · gap 10px · justify-content center. A WRAPPING row, not
     a grid — there is no track count here to collapse at 900px, which is why
     this section owns no column query. It is a real <ul> for the semantics; the
     list chrome is stripped here and role="list" on the element puts the
     semantics back for Safari/VoiceOver (R9). */
  .sip-area-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    justify-content: center;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 26px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  /* THE CHIP. Design: #FFF7F2 ground · radius 100px · padding 11px 18px ·
     13.5px · 600 · #241A22. The design separates its two cells with a literal
     space in the markup; an inline-flex gap of .3em puts the same space in the
     same place while letting the time be guarded independently — a place-only
     row prints no trailing space. The inner wrap plus overflow-wrap is what
     keeps a long owner-typed place inside the pill at 360px rather than widening
     the document (R8).
     LINE-HEIGHT IS THE ONE VALUE HERE THAT IS NOT THE DESIGN'S, and it is
     declared rather than inherited on purpose: the design writes none on the
     chip AND none on its body, so its pill renders at the browser's `normal`,
     while PageBO's body sets 1.72 and would inherit straight into this pill and
     inflate a one-line chip. 1.5 is stated as the closest deliberate value that
     still leaves a WRAPPED second line room — which the design's single-line
     inline span never has to have. It is flat at every width; no query restates
     it. */
  .sip-area-chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0 .3em;
    max-width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    list-style: none;
    background-color: var(--paper);
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    padding: 11px 18px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  /* The place inherits the pill's 13.5px/600/--ink; only the wrap guard is its
     own. The time is the design's purple 700 — the one place in this section the
     brand colour appears as small text, and it appears on the CREAM pill (5.63),
     never straight on the lilac. No font-family: the design leaves it on Nunito
